diagnosis_text:
A thorough end-to-end diagnostic pass found no fault in the IT department's network. The IT machines (it_hod, it_lab1–4 on 192.168.1.x) are fully reachable and can reach all other network segments. Specifically: all IT hosts have correctly configured IPv4 addresses (192.168.1.2–.6), a valid default gateway (192.168.1.1 on router0.eth0), and no ACL or traffic-control rules blocking their traffic. Switch0, the L2 bridge connecting lan_it to the router0 uplink, is healthy — both bridge ports are in STP forwarding state, ebtables is empty, and the FDB has learned the MAC addresses of both router0 and the IT machines. The RIP routing fabric correctly distributes the 192.168.1.0/24 prefix to router1 and router2, and the return paths from all other subnets back to the IT segment are also present. Bidirectional ICMP tests — both from IT machines outbound and from office_pc inbound — complete with 0% packet loss. The switch0 journalctl is empty and carrier-change counters are zero, providing no evidence of a past crash or link flap. The empty /etc/resolv.conf observed on IT machines is topology-wide (present on office_pc, cs_hod, and all sampled hosts), making it baseline lab design rather than an injected fault. The helpdesk complaint cannot be confirmed by any current or historical evidence; the IT department's LAN infrastructure is operating normally.
=== END ===